{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791374999,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100720095012646dcaa87a4340\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I need to finish the turn. Let me summarize progress so far and continue next turn.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_2026100720095012646dcaa87a4340\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"I have diagnosed the root cause and already taken the first steps. Status:\\n\\n**Cause found** \u2014 `zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced` is brace-count blind. When the model's first tool call contains `\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"... lv_open = '{'. ...\\\\\\\"}\\\"`, the escaped `{` inside the JSON string value is counted as an opener that never closes. The depth counter never reaches 0 inside the entry, so `split_entries` clamps `lv_end` to the end of the array and swallows everything after the first call: the `\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` suffix and the entire second entry. `extract_balanced( arguments )` then behaves the same, so the arguments arrive with trailing junk. The fix is string-awareness: skip over `\\\"...\\\"` spans (including `\\\\\\\"` escapes) both in `extract_balanced` and in the depth scan of `split_entries`.\\n\\n**Done so far:** re-read the parser, ran the baseline suite (only the known-red `ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR` fails, 29/30 green), and written the new test include with red regression tests for both `split_entries` and `extract_balanced` (`SPLIT_UNBALANCED_BRACE_IN_STRING`, `BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING`, `BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING`). Activation is publish-pending.\\n\\n**Next turn:** run tests to confirm the new tests are red, then fix the two methods, activate, and show green.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_2026100720095012646dcaa87a4340\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":9153,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":8960},\"output_tokens\":338,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":18},\"total_tokens\":9491}}
