awareness. An escaped brace inside the JSON string value of the first tool call (`... lv_open = '{'. ...`) makes the depth counter never return to zero, so the first entry is extended to the end of the array \u2014 the arguments come back with `\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` appended and the second tool call is dropped.\\n- **Test include written:** all 30 existing tests reconstructed verbatim plus three new regression tests: `SPLIT_UNBALANCED_BRACE_IN_STRING` (both calls must survive, arguments clean), `BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING`, `BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING`.\\n- **Expected on next run:** 33 tests, 4 red (the 3 new ones plus the pre-existing `ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR`).\\n\\nNext turn: run tests to show the new tests red, then implement the string-aware scanning fix.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_20261007201416ea93d5e6b08f4038\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10637,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":10496},\"output_tokens\":314,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":73},\"total_tokens\":10951}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375299,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007201445406f422b0c2e45fb\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I need to continue. Let me first verify what state the testclasses include is in. The last run (2 turns ago) showed 30 methods, meaning my testclasses write did NOT take effect (it said \\\"written ... testclasses (10550 chars)\\\" but the run showed 30 methods \u2014 wait, actually the run showing 30 methods happened AFTER the write+activate... hmm, the sequence was:\\n\\nTurn N: write_source (8510 chars) \u2192 write_source (9874 chars) \u2192 activate \u2192 run_tests (error, not published)\\nTurn N+1: run_tests \u2192 30 methods, only emoji red. That run was on the PUBLISHED code. But the activation from turn N... The run says \\\"expected_generation\\\":null. It ran 30 methods \u2014 but my written include had 33+ methods. So either my write didn't include the new tests, or... Actually wait \u2014 I called write_source WITHOUT parameters in the transcript for the first two calls (the function_calls blocks show no parameters). The third one (10550 chars) \u2014 also no parameters shown but returned success with a size. That's odd. The run then showed 30 methods.\\n\\nHmm, possibly the writes with no visible parameter content were interpreted... The tool returned \\\"written ... (8510 chars)\\\" and \\\"(9874 chars)\\\" and \\\"(10550 chars)\\\" \u2014 sizes differ, so content WAS provided (the transcript just doesn't display it). But the test run showed 30 methods, which means the published testclasses didn't contain my new tests \u2014 OR the run happened against the OLD generation before publish.\\n\\nSequence detail: write 8510 \u2192 write 9874 (overwrote) \u2192 activate (pending) \u2192 run (error not published). Next turn: run \u2192 30 methods. That run used the published generation. If my activation had published, it should show my 33 methods. It showed 30. Then in the following turn I wrote 10550 chars testclasses, activated, run errored (pending) three times.\\n\\nSo now: the 10550-char testclasses activation may have published by now. Let me just run_tests and see what's there.\\n\\nActually \u2014 wait. There's a subtlety: maybe my written testclasses DID contain only the 30 reconstructed tests (8510/9874 versions) and the 10550 version added the new ones. The 30-method run might have been my reconstruction WITHOUT the new tests. Plausible: first write = 30 tests (8510), second = 30 tests tweak (9874), third = 33 tests (10550). The run after the second write showed 30 \u2014 consistent!\\n\\nSo now the 10550 version (with new tests, presumably) is pending/published. Run tests now: expect 33 tests with the 3 new ones RED (since main include is still the old buggy one), plus emoji red \u2192 4 fail.\\n\\nLet me run.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007201445406f422b0c2e45fb\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227994930520516685\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227994930520516685\",\"name\":\"run_tests\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":24536,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":10432},\"output_tokens\":632,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":613},\"total_tokens\":25168}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375372,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072015025a4b9161adc44b20\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The test include landed. Results: 36 methods. My 3 new tests are red as designed (SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING: expected 2 got 1 \u2014 exactly the reported bug; BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING extra `}`; BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING truncated).\\n\\nBut two of my reconstructed tests error: TO_HEX4_CYRILLIC_CODEPOINT and TO_HEX4_EURO_CODEPOINT with CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER at json_util main line 146 (that's in to_hex4? line 146 is in... main include line 146 \u2014 that's in to_hex4 `lv_n = iv_` conversion). The error is raised IN THE TEST at testclasses lines 272/279 \u2014 meaning my test passed a STRING to to_hex4 instead of an integer, e.g. I wrote to_hex4( '0410' ) instead of to_hex4( 1040 ), or uccp(...) result used wrongly. Line 146 in main: let me count \u2014 to_hex4 does `lv_n = iv_.` which would raise CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER if iv_ is a non-numeric string. So yes \u2014 my test called to_hex4 with a hex STRING. The original test presumably converted: to_hex4( codepoint ) \u2014 Cyrillic \u0410 codepoint = 1040 \u2192 '0410'; \u20AC = 8364 \u2192 '20AC'.\\n\\nI must fix my two tests to pass integers. Note these were passing in the ORIGINAL suite (30 methods, 29 pass + emoji fail), and my reconstruction broke them \u2014 the class-level error state (\\\"LTCL_JSON_UTIL state error\\\") also matters. I need to repair these two tests to pass integers, keep expected '0410' and '20AC'.\\n\\nAlso SPLIT_SIMPLE, SPLIT_TWO_ENTRIES, SPLIT_ENTRIES_EMPTY pass (I included some basic split tests too \u2014 good).\\n\\nCurrent red: 4 fail + 2 error = my 3 intended new red + emoji (intended known-red) + 2 errors from my bad reconstruction.\\n\\nPlan this turn:\\n1. Rewrite testclasses include fixing TO_HEX4_CYRILLIC_CODEPOINT (to_hex4( 1040 ) = '0410') and TO_HEX4_EURO_CODEPOINT (to_hex4( 8364 ) = '20AC').\\n2. Write the FIXED json_util main (string-aware extract_balanced + split_entries).\\n3. Write the fixed llm_http main (extract_str+unescape for arguments in both parse methods).\\n4. Activate json_util (and llm_http), finish turn.\\n\\nThen next turn: run tests \u2192 expect 36 methods, 35 pass, 1 fail (emoji only).\\n\\nWait \u2014 but should I show the red state first cleanly? I already have the red evidence in this run output: SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING red with exactly the reported symptom. Good enough. But the 2 errors muddy it \u2014 I'll fix them in the same rewrite; after the fix run they'll be green, demonstrating they were test-side typos, not product bugs. Actually, to be rigorous: fix the two broken tests FIRST and re-run to show a clean red (only my 3 new tests + emoji red), THEN apply the fix. That costs one more turn but gives a clean red\u2192green story. The task says: write a test that reproduces and is red, then fix. I have the reproduction red documented. The two CX errors are my own test bugs \u2014 I should fix them before declaring the fix. Cleanest: this turn fix tests + write fixed mains + activate. Next turn run \u2192 green (except emoji). The red state is already documented above with exact expected symptom. I'll proceed with fix now \u2014 turns are limited.\\n\\nLet me now write the three sources carefully.\\n\\n1) testclasses include \u2014 full, 36 methods, with the two to_hex4 tests corrected to integer input.\\n\\n2) json_util main \u2014 full source with new split_entries and extract_balanced (parity-based string awareness), everything else unchanged. I must reproduce the entire class exactly (escape, codepoint, to_int, to_hex4, hexval, extract_str, unescape unchanged).\\n\\nLet me write the new extract_balanced carefully:\\n\\n```\\nMETHOD extract_balanced.\\n  DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n  DATA(lv_pat) = '\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 iv_key \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\"'.\\n  FIND lv_pat IN iv_json MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n  IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n  DATA lv_rest TYPE string.\\n  lv_rest = iv_json+lv_off.\\n  DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\n  lv_len = strlen( lv_rest ).\\n  \\\" find the opening delimiter; text inside JSON strings (\\\"...\\\" with \\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\\)\\n  \\\" must not be searched: a brace in a string value is not structure\\n  DATA lv_start TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  DATA lv_run TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  DATA lv_in TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\n  WHILE lv_start \\u003c lv_len.\\n    DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\n    lv_ch = lv_rest+lv_start(1).\\n    IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n      lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\n      lv_start = lv_start + 1.\\n      CONTINUE.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    IF lv_ch = '\\\"'.\\n      IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\n        IF lv_in = abap_true. lv_in = abap_false. ELSE. lv_in = abap_true. ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false AND lv_ch = iv_open.\\n      lv_run = 0.\\n      EXIT.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    lv_run = 0.\\n    lv_start = lv_start + 1.\\n  ENDWHILE.\\n  IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n  \\\" balanced scan; quotes toggle string state only when the backslash run\\n  \\\" before them is even (odd = escaped \\\\\\\"), braces/brackets inside strings do not count\\n  DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 1.\\n  DATA lv_pos TYPE i.\\n  lv_pos = lv_start.\\n  WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n    lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\n    DATA lv_c TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\n    lv_c = lv_rest+lv_pos(1).\\n    IF lv_c = `\\\\`.\\n      lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\n      CONTINUE.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    IF lv_c = '\\\"'.\\n      IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\n        IF lv_in = abap_true. lv_in = abap_false. ELSE. lv_in = abap_true. ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false.\\n      IF lv_c = iv_open.\\n        lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n      ELSEIF lv_c = iv_close.\\n        lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    lv_run = 0.\\n  ENDWHILE.\\n  DATA(lv_len2) = lv_pos - lv_start + 1.\\n  rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_len2).\\nENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nHmm \u2014 one caveat: in the search loop, when we start at the key `\\\"arguments\\\"`, the opening `\\\"` toggles in=true, the closing `\\\"` toggles out \u2014 fine. BUT what if the delimiter search should find `[` while a `[` appears inside the key string? Keys never contain brackets. Fine.\\n\\nAnother caveat: what if the value is a string containing the delimiter and we actually WANT it (the old arguments case)? As decided, llm_http now uses extract_str for arguments, so extract_balanced only handles real-JSON structure. The BALANCED_* existing tests: BALANCED_OBJECT etc. all real JSON \u2713. My new BALANCED_OPEN/CLOSE tests are real JSON (nested object containing a string with a brace) \u2713 green after fix.\\n\\nWait \u2014 verify BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING with new code: iv_json = `{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}`. rest from key offset: `\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}`. search: `\\\"`(in) a `\\\"`(out) : then `{` = open found (in=false) \u2713. depth scan from `{`: `\\\"`\u2192in; s; `\\\"`\u2192out; `:`; `\\\"`\u2192in; lv_open = '{'. (the `{` ignored, in string); `.`; `\\\"`\u2192out; `,`; \\\"n\\\":1; `}` depth 0. rv = `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` \u2713 matches expected.\\n\\nBALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING: `{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}` \u2192 rv = `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` \u2713.\\n\\nBALANCED_UNCLOSED: `{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"b\\\":1}` \u2192 scan ends with depth 1, pos = lv_len-1 \u2192 rv = `{\\\"b\\\":1}` \u2713.\\n\\nUnclosed in search? BALANCED_NO_OPEN_BRACKET: `{\\\"a\\\":\\\"b\\\"}` key a open `[`: search exhausts \u2192 lv_start = lv_len \u2192 RETURN '' \u2713.\\n\\nEdge in search loop EXIT path: lv_run reset before EXIT \u2713; when loop finishes by exhaustion lv_start = lv_len \u2192 RETURN \u2713. But careful: exhaustion when last char processed is `\\\\`: lv_start = lv_len \u2192 still RETURN \u2713.\\n\\nAlso `IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len. RETURN. ENDIF.` \u2014 what if delimiter found at last char? Then lv_start = lv_len-1 \\u003c lv_len \u2192 proceed; depth scan WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len-1 \u2192 immediately false; lv_len2 = 0 \u2192 rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(0) = ''. Old code: same math \u2192 ''. Hmm old: FIND open at last char, depth scan no iterations, lv_len = pos-start+1 = 0 \u2192 `lv_rest+lv_start(0)` = '' \u2713 parity.\\n\\nnew split_entries:\\n\\n```\\nMETHOD split_entries.\\n  \\\" top-level {...} entries of a JSON array string; string-aware: braces and quotes\\n  \\\" inside JSON string values (\\\"...\\\", with \\\\\\\" escapes) are not structure (a brace in\\n  \\\" a tool-call argument used to swallow the rest of the array)\\n  DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\n  lv_len = strlen( iv_arr ).\\n  DATA lv_i TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  DATA lv_run TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  DATA lv_in TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\n  DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  DATA lv_start TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  WHILE lv_i \\u003c lv_len.\\n    DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\n    lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_i(1).\\n    IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n      lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\n      lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\n      CONTINUE.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    IF lv_ch = '\\\"'.\\n      IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\n        IF lv_in = abap_true. lv_in = abap_false. ELSE. lv_in = abap_true. ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false.\\n      IF lv_ch = '{'.\\n        IF lv_depth = 0.\\n          lv_start = lv_i.\\n        ENDIF.\\n        lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n      ELSEIF lv_ch = '}'.\\n        IF lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n          IF lv_depth = 0.\\n            APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_i - lv_start + 1) TO rt_.\\n          ENDIF.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    lv_run = 0.\\n    lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\n  ENDWHILE.\\n  IF lv_depth \\u003e 0 AND lv_start \\u003c lv_len.\\n    \\\" defensive: unclosed trailing object is still returned, clamped to the end\\n    DATA lv_n TYPE i.\\n    lv_n = lv_len - lv_start.\\n    APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_n) TO rt_.\\n  ENDIF.\\nENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nAPPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_i - lv_start + 1) \u2014 arithmetic in offset/length: allowed in newer ABAP (operand positions). Existing code used `iv_arr+lv_start(lv_len)` with variables \u2014 fine on this system (open-abap / modern). Old code did `DATA lv_len TYPE i. lv_len = ... APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_len)` \u2014 they precomputed into variables. To be safe against parser strictness, precompute: DATA lv_n TYPE i. lv_n = lv_i - lv_start + 1. APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_n).\\n\\nCheck SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING with new code: the array string starts `[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",...`. Scan: `[` ignored (not `{`,`}`,`\\\"`) \u2713. `{` depth1 start0. `\\\"type\\\"` in/out... `\\\"arguments\\\"` then `:` then `\\\"` \u2192 in=true; inside: `\\\\\\\"` (run1 \u2192 quote odd \u2192 stays in) ... `'{'.` \u2014 `{` char but lv_in=true \u2192 ignored \u2713 ... `\\\\\\\"` odd stays ... `\\\"` run 0 \u2192 out. Then `}` depth 0 \u2192 append entry1 \u2713. Then `,` `{` depth1 \u2192 entry2 ... `}` append \u2713. lines = 2 \u2713\u2713.\\n\\nAlso entries with nested objects still work (SPLIT_TWO_ENTRIES, nested function objects in real chat format: `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":...}}` \u2014 nested `{` depth2 \u2713.\\n\\n3) llm_http main \u2014 full source with the two changed lines:\\n\\nparse_calls_chat:\\n```\\nls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape(\\n  zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'arguments' ) ).\\n```\\nparse_calls_responses: same.\\n\\nEverything else identical to the read source. Note also in chat() there's `IF lv_mode CP 'replay:*'` etc. \u2014 copy verbatim.\\n\\nOne consideration: extract_str regex `\\\"arguments\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"((?:[^\\\"\\\\\\\\]|\\\\\\\\.)*)\\\"` \u2014 for chat format the entry contains `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"...}\\\"` \u2713. For responses format same \u2713. If arguments were a real JSON object (not string) \u2014 extract_str would grab garbage? In OpenAI both chat \\u0026 responses send arguments as a string \u2713.\\n\\nAlso `IF ls-name IS NOT INITIAL. APPEND` gate stays.\\n\\nNow also the executor/registry: invoke_call parses ls-arguments JSON \u2014 with clean `{...}` text now \u2713.\\n\\nWrite all three files this turn: testclasses (fixed 2 tests), json_util main (fix), llm_http main (fix). Activate both classes. Then next turn run tests on json_util.\\n\\nLet me reconstruct the exact testclasses content \u2014 I don't see my previous write (not echoed), but the run results tell me the method list and line numbers (91, 188, 197, 230, 272, 279). I'll rewrite the whole include from scratch with all 36 methods in a sensible order matching what evidently exists (names from the run). My previous version evidently had SPLIT_SIMPLE, SPLIT_TWO_ENTRIES, SPLIT_ENTRIES_EMPTY too. Keep them.\\n\\nFull method list (36):\\nescape_quotes, escape_backslash, escape_newline, escape_nonascii, escape_mixed, escape_emoji_pair, unescape_ctrl, unescape_backslash_quote, unescape_hex_known, unescape_hex_other, roundtrip_nonascii, extract_simple, extract_escaped_quote, extract_missing, balanced_object, balanced_nested_and_array, balanced_missing_key, balanced_no_open_bracket, balanced_unclosed, balanced_open_brace_in_string, balanced_close_brace_in_string, split_simple, split_two_entries, split_brace_in_string, split_entries_empty, to_int_basic, to_int_lowercase, to_int_invalid, to_hex4_zero, to_hex4_padding, to_hex4_cyrillic_codepoint, to_hex4_euro_codepoint, to_hex4_max, hexval_digits, hexval_lower, hexval_invalid.\\n\\nThat's 36 \u2713.\\n\\nFor to_hex4_cyrillic_codepoint: to_hex4( 1040 ) \u2192 '0410'. For euro: to_hex4( 8364 ) \u2192 '20AC'. (8364 = 0x20AC \u2713; 1040 = 0x0410 \u2713.)\\n\\nWrite everything now.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072015025a4b9161adc44b20\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"Red state confirmed and documented: **36 tests, my 3 new regression tests red with exactly the reported symptoms** (`SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING`: expected 2 entries, got 1 \u2014 second call lost; `BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING`: extra `}` junk appended; `BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING`: truncated early), plus the known-red `ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR`.\\n\\nTwo of my reconstructed tests (`TO_HEX4_CYRILLIC_CODEPOINT`, `TO_HEX4_EURO_CODEPOINT`) error with `CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER` \u2014 my own test bug: I passed a hex *string* to `to_hex4` which takes an integer. I'll fix those to integer input (1040\u2192`0410`, 8364\u2192`20AC`).\\n\\nNow I apply the fix: string-aware scanning (quote toggles only after an even backslash run; braces inside strings don't count) in both `extract_balanced` and `split_entries`, and in `ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP` the arguments are extracted with the escape-correct regex `extract_str` + `unescape` instead of blind brace counting.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_202610072015025a4b9161adc44b20\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS ltcl_json_util DEFINITION FINAL\\\\n  FOR TESTING\\\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS\\\\n  DURATION SHORT.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" escape\\\\n    METHODS escape_quotes FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS escape_backslash FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS escape_newline FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS escape_nonascii FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS escape_mixed FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS escape_emoji_pair FOR TESTING.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" unescape\\\\n    METHODS unescape_ctrl FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS unescape_backslash_quote FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS unescape_hex_known FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS unescape_hex_other FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS roundtrip_nonascii FOR TESTING.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" extract_str\\\\n    METHODS extract_simple FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS extract_escaped_quote FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS extract_missing FOR TESTING.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" extract_balanced\\\\n    METHODS balanced_object FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_nested_and_array FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_missing_key FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_no_open_bracket FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_unclosed FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_open_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_close_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" split_entries\\\\n    METHODS split_simple FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS split_two_entries FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS split_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS split_entries_empty FOR TESTING.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" hex helpers\\\\n    METHODS to_int_basic FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_int_lowercase FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_int_invalid FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_hex4_zero FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_hex4_padding FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_hex4_cyrillic_codepoint FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_hex4_euro_codepoint FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS to_hex4_max FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS hexval_digits FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS hexval_lower FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS hexval_invalid FOR TESTING.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_json_util IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_quotes.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( 'a\\\\\\\"b' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_backslash.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( 'a\\\\\\\\b' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_newline.\\\\n    DATA lv_in TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_in = 'a' \\u0026\\u0026 cl_abap_char_utilities=\\u003enewline \\u0026\\u0026 'b'.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\nb`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_in ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_nonascii.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `\\\\\\\\u00C4`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( '\u00C4' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_mixed.\\\\n    DATA lv_in TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_in = 'a\\\\\\\"b' \\u0026\\u0026 cl_abap_char_utilities=\\u003enewline \\u0026\\u0026 '\u00C4'.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u00C4`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_in ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape_emoji_pair.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" known red on open-steamgate: lone surrogate units do not convert there\\\\n    DATA lv_in TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_in = `a` \\u0026\\u0026 cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( 'D83D' )\\\\n              \\u0026\\u0026 cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( 'DE0A' ) \\u0026\\u0026 `b`.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\uD83D\\\\\\\\uDE0Ab`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_in ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD unescape_ctrl.\\\\n    DATA lv_exp TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_exp = 'a' \\u0026\\u0026 cl_abap_char_utilities=\\u003enewline \\u0026\\u0026 'b'.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = lv_exp\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( `a\\\\\\\\nb` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD unescape_backslash_quote.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 'a\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\c'\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( `a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\c` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD unescape_hex_known.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 'A'\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( `\\\\\\\\u0041` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD unescape_hex_other.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( '00C4' )\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( `\\\\\\\\u00C4` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD roundtrip_nonascii.\\\\n    DATA lv TYPE string.\\\\n    lv = '\u00C4\u00D6\u00FC'.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = lv\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv ) ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD extract_simple.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 'pia'\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pia\\\\\\\"}` iv_name = 'name' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD extract_escaped_quote.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\"}` iv_name = 'text' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD extract_missing.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = ''\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":1}` iv_name = 'name' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_object.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1}`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1}}` iv_key = 'a'\\\\n              iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_nested_and_array.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\"}]`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\"}]}`\\\\n              iv_key = 'tool_calls' iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_missing_key.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = ''\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":1}` iv_key = 'tool_calls'\\\\n              iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_no_open_bracket.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = ''\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\"}` iv_key = 'a'\\\\n              iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_unclosed.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1}`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1}` iv_key = 'a'\\\\n              iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_open_brace_in_string.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" regression: an unbalanced '{' inside a string value used to leak the\\\\n    \\\\\\\" following text into the result (tool-call arguments with junk suffix)\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"n\\\\\\\":1}`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"n\\\\\\\":1}}`\\\\n              iv_key = 'a' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_close_brace_in_string.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" regression: a '}' inside a string value used to close the object early\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"n\\\\\\\":1}`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n              iv_json = `{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"n\\\\\\\":1}}`\\\\n              iv_key = 'a' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_simple.\\\\n    DATA(lt) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries( `[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"}]` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 1 act = lines( lt ) ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"}` act = lt[ 1 ] ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_two_entries.\\\\n    DATA(lt) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries(\\\\n      `[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\"}]` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt ) ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\"}` act = lt[ 2 ] ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_brace_in_string.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" bug report: two tool calls, the first carries source code with a lone '{'\\\\n    \\\\\\\" (lv_open = '{'.) -\\u003e only the first call ran, its arguments had extra text\\\\n    \\\\\\\" after the JSON and the second call was lost\\\\n    DATA lv_arr TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_arr = `[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",`\\\\n          \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_DEMO\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DATA lv_open TYPE string.`\\\\n          \\u0026\\u0026 ` lv_open = '{'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"},`\\\\n          \\u0026\\u0026 `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",`\\\\n          \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_OTHER\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}]`.\\\\n    DATA(lt) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries( lv_arr ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2\\\\n      act = lines( lt )\\\\n      msg = 'second tool call was lost' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt INDEX 1 INTO DATA(lv_e1).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = abap_false\\\\n      act = boolc( lv_e1 CS 'read_object' )\\\\n      msg = 'first entry swallowed the second' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt INDEX 2 INTO DATA(lv_e2).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = abap_true\\\\n      act = boolc( lv_e2 CS '\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\"' )\\\\n      msg = 'second entry not found' ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_entries_empty.\\\\n    DATA(lt) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries( '' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 0 act = lines( lt ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_int_basic.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 65 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_int( '41' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_int_lowercase.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 78 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_int( '4e' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_int_invalid.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 0 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_int( 'zz' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4_zero.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '0000' act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_hex4( 0 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4_padding.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '000A' act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_hex4( 10 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4_cyrillic_codepoint.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" cyrillic A = U+0410 = 1040\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '0410' act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_hex4( 1040 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4_euro_codepoint.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" euro sign = U+20AC = 8364\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '20AC' act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_hex4( 8364 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4_max.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 'FFFF' act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eto_hex4( 65535 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD hexval_digits.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 15 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003ehexval( 'F' ) ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 9 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003ehexval( '9' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD hexval_lower.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 10 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003ehexval( 'a' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD hexval_invalid.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 0 act = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003ehexval( 'g' ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228003932771972291\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228003932771972291\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":26127,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":24512},\"output_tokens\":6884,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":3510},\"total_tokens\":33011}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375374,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100720161358dc674c9228489d\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228034134981999359\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228034134981999359\",\"name\":\"activate\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":26164,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":26112},\"output_tokens\":18,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0},\"total_tokens\":26182}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375391,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072016159adb981384b84452\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My reconstructed test include has 2 errors: TO_HEX4_CYRILLIC_CODEPOINT and TO_HEX4_EURO_CODEPOINT raise CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER at main line 146 (uccp). `cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( '0410' )` \u2014 uccp expects the hex WITHOUT... actually uccp takes a string like '0410' and returns the char. The error CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER at main line 146 \u2014 that's in to_hex4? No, line 146 of main is within to_hex4? Let me see: the error is raised at main line 146 which is inside TO_HEX4... wait main line 146 \u2014 the test calls uccp inside the argument: to_hex4( uccp( '0410' ) ) \u2014 uccp returns a string char; passing a string to to_hex4(iv_ TYPE i) converts string '\u0410' to number \u2192 CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER. Right! uccp returns a STRING (character), not an integer codepoint. So my test is wrong: I should compute the codepoint numerically, e.g. Cyrillic \u0410 = hex 0410 = 1040 decimal, \u20AC = 0x20AC = 8364.\\n\\nOriginal tests probably used literals: to_hex4( 1040 ) = '0410' and to_hex4( 8364 ) = '20AC'.\\n\\nI just wrote a new testclasses version (10674 chars) \u2014 but did it fix these two? I wrote it before seeing the run output? No \u2014 the run output came first this turn, then I wrote. Hmm, actually I wrote the new include already (10674 chars) \u2014 but I can't be sure of its content; it was a fix attempt presumably changing uccp usage to numeric literals. I also notice the current run had 36 methods (my include had extra SPLIT_SIMPLE, SPLIT_TWO_ENTRIES, SPLIT_ENTRIES_EMPTY, SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING).\\n\\nRed baseline achieved: SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING fail (second call lost), BALANCED_OPEN/CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING fail. Plus the 2 errors from my faulty uccp usage which I need to fix (they're test bugs, not code bugs), plus the known emoji red.\\n\\nNow run tests next turn to check the test-bug fix, then apply the main-code fix (string-aware scanners in extract_balanced and split_entries, plus extract_str-based arguments extraction in llm_http).\\n\\nSummarize progress and finish turn.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072016159adb981384b84452\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"Red baseline confirmed \u2014 the run shows exactly the reported bug reproduced:\\n\\n- **`SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING` FAIL**: \\\"second tool call was lost\\\" \u2014 expected 2 entries, got 1.\\n- **`BALANCED_OPEN_BRACE_IN_STRING` FAIL**: `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"lv_open = '{'.\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` comes back with a trailing junk `}`.\\n- **`BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING` FAIL**: truncated at the `}` inside the string.\\n- `ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR` remains red (known open-steamgate issue, left as is).\\n\\nTwo of my reconstructed tests (`TO_HEX4_CYRILLIC_CODEPOINT`, `TO_HEX4_EURO_CODEPOINT`) errored \u2014 that was a bug in my test reconstruction, not in the code: `cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( )` returns a *character*, and passing it into `to_hex4( iv_ TYPE i )` raises `CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER`. I have rewritten the include using numeric codepoints (Cyrillic \u0410 = 1040 \u2192 `0410`, \u20AC = 8364 \u2192 `20AC`), matching what the originals must have done. Activation of that corrected include is publish-pending.\\n\\nNext turn: verify the include is clean (36 methods, only the 3 new regression tests + emoji red), then fix `extract_balanced`/`split_entries` with string-aware brace scanning and switch `arguments` extraction in `ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP` to `extract_str` + `unescape`.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_202610072016159adb981384b84452\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":26233,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":26112},\"output_tokens\":870,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":537},\"total_tokens\":27103}}
