{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375559,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072019057dbbc3afd2c0459d\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The tests still show the same failures \u2014 the activation was publish-pending when I ran. The run says \\\"RED tests ran\\\" with identical results to before. Two possibilities:\\n1. The activation of my fixed main include wasn't published when this run executed (the run may have used the previous generation).\\n2. My write of the main include didn't actually contain the fix.\\n\\nWait \u2014 in the previous turn I did: write testclasses, write main, write llm_http main, activate json_util, activate llm_http. The activation said publish pending. Then this turn's run_tests executed... and results are identical to the red run. Hmm, but the publish should have completed between turns. Unless my write_source calls for the main include accidentally wrote the OLD code? I can't see what I wrote \u2014 the calls in the transcript show empty invoke blocks (the content isn't displayed), but they reported \\\"written ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (11180 chars)\\\".\\n\\nHmm, 11180 chars for the main. The original main... unknown length. My new main with fixes should be around that.\\n\\nWait, but the test results are byte-identical failures including same line numbers in testclasses (92, 195, 204, 240) as the previous run. If my new main include had been published and contained the fix, split_brace_in_string would pass. Unless the fix I wrote has a bug \u2014 e.g., my string-aware logic doesn't work. Identical failure messages suggest the OLD main code is still running.\\n\\nPossibility: the run_tests ran against the published generation, but my activation from last turn (op_id=21b8cc43...) was still pending when this turn started, and the tool note says \\\"new code becomes live in the NEXT step\\\". The run_tests happened as the first step of this turn \u2014 maybe the publish lands only after another operation? Earlier in the session I saw the same pattern: after \\\"publish pending\\\", the next turn's run_tests sometimes still said \\\"activation not published yet\\\" repeatedly. So the publish seems to lag arbitrarily.\\n\\nLet me just try running tests again now \u2014 if still same, I need to verify what's in the main include by reading it back. Actually the safest: read_object json_util to check whether the fix is in the source, and run tests again. If the source shows the fix but tests fail identically, then publish lag or my fix logic is wrong \u2014 I'd then debug the logic.\\n\\nPlan: read_object ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (check fix present), then run_tests. Read first \u2014 independent calls can be batched, but run_tests result interpretation depends on read. Still, they're independent operations; batching is allowed. But ordering within a block: they say make independent calls in the same block. read_object + run_tests are independent. Let me do both.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072019057dbbc3afd2c0459d\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228031214404239125\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228031214404239125\",\"name\":\"read_object\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228031214404239124\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228031214404239124\",\"name\":\"run_tests\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":33660,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":32256},\"output_tokens\":624,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":588},\"total_tokens\":34284}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375654,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007201922201cb42415214065\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The read_object shows the FIXED main include is written (the new string-aware split_entries and extract_balanced are there). But the tests still show the old behavior \u2014 3 new tests still red. Why? The test run says \\\"generation_id\\\":\\\"7a68c5ffe680388b\\\" \u2014 same generation as the previous run. So the activation hasn't published yet \u2014 the tests ran against the OLD published code.\\n\\nWait \u2014 I activated both classes last turn, and the run still shows old behavior. The generation_id is identical to the previous run (7a68c5ffe680388b vs previous 7a68c5ffe680388b? Previous was \\\"7a68c5ffe680388b\\\" \u2014 actually the previous run showed \\\"generation_id\\\":\\\"7a68c5ffe680388b\\\"... let me check: the run before showed generation 7a68c5ffe680388b? It showed \\\"generation_id\\\":\\\"7a68c5ffe680388b\\\". Hmm, the run at the start of this turn showed cccc6ced41226f6a. Then the latest run shows 7a68c5ffe680388b. So generation changed \u2014 new code SHOULD be active... but the tests still fail with the same values.\\n\\nHmm wait. The read shows the new main include. But the tests still fail as if old code runs. That means my fixed implementation has a BUG \u2014 it behaves like the old one for these cases?! Let me trace carefully.\\n\\nHmm \u2014 CRITICAL BUG: In extract_balanced, I use `lv_run` and `lv_in` \u2014 but there's a subtle issue: in the depth-scan loop, when `lv_in` is true and we hit `\\\\`, we do `lv_run = lv_run + 1. CONTINUE.` \u2014 the CONTINUE skips `lv_run = 0` at the end \u2014 good, that's intended (accumulate run). When we hit any other char, `lv_run = 0` resets \u2014 good.\\n\\nWait, but there's a REAL bug: in the depth scan loop, after processing `\\\\` we CONTINUE \u2014 but we did NOT reset lv_run; correct. For quotes: `IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0` \u2192 toggle. For a quote preceded by 1 backslash (odd) \u2192 no toggle \u2713.\\n\\nLet me trace BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING: iv_json = `{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}`, key 'a', open '{', close '}'.\\n\\nlv_off: FIND `\\\"a\\\"` \u2014 where does `\\\"a\\\"` first occur? The string `{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}` \u2014 FIND `\\\"a\\\"` matches at offset 1. lv_rest = `\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}` (len 19).\\n\\nSearch loop:\\n- lv_start=0: `\\\"` run0 even \u2192 toggle in=true. lv_start=1.\\n- 'a' \u2192 nothing (not quote, not open since in=true... wait the ELSIF: `ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false AND lv_ch = iv_open` \u2014 in=true so skip). lv_start=2.\\n- `\\\"` run0 \u2192 toggle in=false. lv_start=3.\\n- ':' \u2192 in=false, not open. lv_start=4.\\n- '{' \u2192 in=false AND = iv_open \u2192 EXIT with lv_start=4. \u2713\\n\\nDepth scan from lv_pos=4, lv_run was reset to 0 before EXIT \u2713, lv_in=false, depth=1:\\n- pos5: `\\\"` run0 even \u2192 in=true.\\n- pos6: 's' in string \u2192 nothing.\\n- pos7: `\\\"` run0 \u2192 in=false.\\n- pos8: ':' nothing.\\n- pos9: `\\\"` \u2192 in=true.\\n- pos10: '}' \u2014 in=true \u2192 the ELSIF `lv_in = abap_false` fails \u2192 ignored \u2713\u2713 (this is the fix!)\\n- pos11: `\\\"` run0 \u2192 in=false.\\n- pos12: ',' nothing.\\n- pos13: `\\\"` in=true. pos14 'n' pos15 `\\\"` out. pos16 ':' pos17 '1'.\\n- pos18: '}' \u2192 in=false \u2192 depth 1-1=0 \u2192 loop ends (lv_pos=18).\\n- lv_len2 = 18-4+1 = 15 \u2192 lv_rest+4(15) = `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` \u2713 CORRECT.\\n\\nSo the fixed code WOULD produce the right result... but the test still fails with the OLD actual value `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}`. Conclusion: the run still executed OLD code. The generation_ids: first run this turn cccc6ced..., second run 7a68c5ffe... \u2014 hmm, second run differs, but both show identical failures. Actually maybe both runs this turn ran before publish? The read_object shows the fixed source is present in the object (inactive version? or active?). read_object reads \\\"the ABAP source of a class\\\" \u2014 probably the inactive version if activation is pending, or the active one.\\n\\nThe activation message said \\\"publish pending \u2014 new code live in next step\\\". I activated at the END of last turn. This turn's first run \u2014 should have been live. Unless the publish takes effect only after another step boundary... The rule from system prompt: \\\"After activate, finish your turn with a summary\\\" and \\\"If the last activation is not published yet, finish your turn and run tests in the next turn.\\\"\\n\\nI did: turn N: activate (pending). Turn N+1 (this turn): ran tests \u2192 still old?? Both runs this turn show old behavior with same failure details and line numbers (195, 204, 240 \u2014 matching the NEW testclasses include positions? The red run before my fix showed lines 188/197/230; after the testclasses fix they became 195/204/240 \u2014 meaning the NEW testclasses WERE active in those runs. And main was still old? But I wrote both and activated both...\\n\\nWait \u2014 last turn I did: write testclasses \u2192 write main (json_util) \u2192 write main (llm_http) \u2192 activate json_util \u2192 activate llm_http. Both pending. This turn run_tests \u2192 json_util. The testclasses changes ARE reflected (line numbers shifted to 195/204/240 and TO_HEX4_* now pass \u2014 those were testclasses fixes!). But the main include changes are NOT reflected?? That's bizarre \u2014 testclasses from the new version active but main from old?\\n\\nHmm, actually NO. Look again: TO_HEX4 tests now pass \u2014 but that could ALSO be because they're in the new testclasses include. And main include \u2014 the failures show old behavior. So: testclasses = new, main = old. How?\\n\\nMaybe the write of main actually failed?? The tool said \\\"written ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL  (11180 chars)\\\". And read_object NOW shows the fixed main. So the fixed main is in the system. But run_tests runs \\\"the local ABAP Unit tests of a class on the published (active) code\\\". Possibly the main include activation didn't publish because... hmm, both were activated with pending status.\\n\\nOR: the publish happens one step after activation, and my two runs this turn were still on the pre-activation generation for MAIN because... the run output says \\\"expected_generation\\\":null. The first run this turn: generation cccc6ced (same as last turn's run). Second run: 7a68c5ffe \u2014 a NEW generation. But results identical (old behavior for main, new line numbers for tests \u2014 wait, line numbers 195/204/240 appeared ALREADY in the cccc6ced run at the start of this turn).\\n\\nHmm wait, let me recheck the timeline:\\n- Turn A (2 turns ago): wrote testclasses (11095 chars) \u2014 the one with fixed TO_HEX4 and line numbers 195/204/240? Then wrote main json_util (11180) and llm_http (10616), activated both.\\n- Turn B (last turn): run \u2192 cccc6ced, 32 pass/4 fail, TO_HEX4 pass, new line numbers, main old behavior.\\n- This turn: run \u2192 7a68c5ffe, same results. Then read+run \u2192 same again.\\n\\nSo even after 2 generation bumps, main behaves old. Something is wrong: maybe my write of main actually didn't change the ACTIVE main because... OR the fix has a real bug that makes it behave identically?? Let me re-examine the actual failure values under the assumption the NEW code ran:\\n\\nBALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING expected `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` got `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}` \u2014 new code per my trace gives the expected. Unless... hmm, wait: `DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.` INSIDE the WHILE loop \u2014 declaring data inside a loop is fine in ABAP (declarations are hoisted). \\n\\nOH WAIT. I see a potential killer bug: `DATA(lv_pat) = ...` etc. fine. But in the depth loop: `IF lv_c = `\\\\`` \u2014 comparing c LENGTH 1 with string literal backtick-backslash-backtick = `\\\\` \u2014 fine.\\n\\nHmm, but actually \u2014 did the testclasses run against a STALE compiled main? The result \\\"state ran\\\" with same failures three times across two generations strongly suggests main really is still old. read_object might show the INACTIVE (edited) version, while the active version is old \u2014 i.e., my activate didn't take effect for main?? But it reported op_id success for the class.\\n\\nAlternatively \u2014 maybe BOTH writes landed: the class main I read is the new one... and the run DID use it, and my new code has a bug making it behave like old. Let me look VERY carefully for such a bug.\\n\\nIn extract_balanced \u2014 OH NO. I see it. The search loop:\\n\\n```\\nIF lv_ch = '\\\"'.\\n  IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0. toggle. ENDIF.\\nELSEIF lv_in = abap_false AND lv_ch = iv_open.\\n```\\n\\nFor BALANCED tests this is fine...\\n\\nHmm wait, actually let me recheck the run results once more: SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING got 1 entry. With new split_entries, the arguments string `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"... '{' ...\\\\\\\"}\\\"` \u2014 trace: `\\\"` before `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"` toggles in=true... wait! The VALUE of arguments starts with `\\\"` then `{` is INSIDE the string. Trace on real entry text:\\n\\n`{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_DEMO\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}`\\n\\n- `{` depth1, start0\\n- `\\\"type\\\"` \u2192 in/out\\n- ..., `\\\"arguments\\\"` \u2192 in then out (even runs)\\n- `:` \\n- `\\\"` \u2192 in=true (run 0 even)\\n- `\\\\` run=1\\n- `\\\"` run1 odd \u2192 NO toggle, stays in \u2713\\n- `{`?? WAIT \u2014 the char after `\\\\\\\"` is `{`? The value starts `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"...` \u2014 order: `{`, then `\\\\`, then `\\\"`, then `name`... Hmm no: `\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":...\\\"` \u2014 the FIRST char after the opening `\\\"` of the value is `{`! So: `\\\"` toggles in=true, then `{` \u2014 but in=true \u2192 ignored \u2713 (that `{` is the arguments object opener inside the string \u2014 correctly ignored for ENTRY splitting!). \\n- `\\\\` `\\\"` odd \u2192 stays in. `name`. `\\\\` `\\\"` odd \u2192 stays. `:`. `\\\\` `\\\"` odd. `ZCL_DEMO`. ... `lv_open = '{'.` \u2014 `{` in=true \u2192 ignored \u2713. ... `\\\\` `\\\"` odd. `}` \u2014 still in string \u2192 ignored \u2713 (this is the arguments object's closing brace, inside the value string).\\n- `\\\"` run0 even \u2192 in=false \u2713 (closing quote of the value string)\\n- `}` \u2192 in=false, depth 1\u21920 \u2192 APPEND entry \u2713\u2713\u2713\\n\\nSo new split_entries gives 2 entries. The test failing with actual=1 means OLD code ran. Definitive.\\n\\nSo the problem: the main include activation is not publishing. Why would testclasses changes publish but not main? Actually \u2014 maybe the testclasses \\\"changes\\\" I attributed to publishing were just... no, line numbers 195/204/240 and passing TO_HEX4 prove new testclasses ran.\\n\\nHmm, one possibility: run_tests runs on \\\"the published (active) code\\\" \u2014 and there may be separate publish for main vs testclasses? Unlikely.\\n\\nAnother possibility: my main-include write DID activate and publish, and read confirms it. But the UNIT TEST process caches? The three runs across generations all old... \\n\\nWait, actually \u2014 maybe generation 7a68c5ffe IS the new code and my trace is wrong somewhere. Let me re-trace BALANCED_CLOSE_BRACE_IN_STRING super carefully against the EXACT code in the read (not my memory):\\n\\n```\\nMETHOD extract_balanced.\\n  FIND lv_pat IN iv_json MATCH OFFSET lv_off.  \\\" \\\"a\\\" found at offset 1\\n  lv_rest = iv_json+lv_off.  \\\" starts at `\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}`\\n  \\\" search loop\\n  WHILE lv_start \\u003c lv_len.\\n    lv_ch = lv_rest+lv_start(1).\\n    IF lv_ch = `\\\\`. ... ENDIF.\\n    IF lv_ch = '\\\"'.\\n      IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\n        toggle\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false AND lv_ch = iv_open.\\n      lv_run = 0. EXIT.\\n    ENDIF.\\n    lv_run = 0.\\n    lv_start = lv_start + 1.\\n  ENDWHILE.\\n```\\n\\nlv_rest = `\\\"a\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}}`, lv_len = 19.\\n- 0: `\\\"` \u2192 run0 even \u2192 toggle \u2192 lv_in=true. start=1\\n- 1: 'a' \u2192 in=true so no open-match. start=2\\n- 2: `\\\"` \u2192 even \u2192 toggle \u2192 false. start=3\\n- 3: ':' \u2192 not open. start=4\\n- 4: '{' \u2192 in=false AND = iv_open \u2192 EXIT, lv_start=4 \u2713 (lv_run=0)\\n\\ndepth: lv_pos=4, depth=1:\\n- WHILE 4 \\u003c 18 AND depth\\u003e0:\\n  - pos5 `\\\"` even \u2192 in=true\\n  - pos6 's'\\n  - pos7 `\\\"` even \u2192 in=false\\n  - pos8 ':'\\n  - pos9 `\\\"` \u2192 in=true\\n  - pos10 '}' \u2192 in=true \u2192 ELSIF fails \u2192 NOT counted \u2713\\n  - pos11 `\\\"` even \u2192 in=false\\n  - pos12 ','\\n  - pos13 `\\\"` in=true; 14 'n'; 15 `\\\"` out; 16 ':'; 17 '1'\\n  - pos18 '}' \u2192 in=false \u2192 depth=0 \u2192 exit\\n- lv_len2 = 18-4+1 = 15 \u2192 substring(4,15) = `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}` \u2713\\n\\nThe code is correct. Expected value in test = `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"n\\\":1}`. So if new code ran, test passes. It failed with EXACTLY the old-code value `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"}`. \u2192 OLD code ran.\\n\\nSo the main include is not published despite activation reporting success. OR \u2014 the run_tests harness ran against the active version and the active version is still old because my write_source for main was somehow to a different include? I called write_source with name ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL, source, and NO include param \u2014 default \\\"main\\\". OK.\\n\\nHmm \u2014 \\\"written ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL  (11180 chars)\\\" \u2014 note: no \\\"(main)\\\" label but default is main. read_object confirms main content is new (read_object probably reads the latest written/active?). \\n\\nGiven the sandbox semantics (\\\"new code live in NEXT step\\\"), and that I activated at the very end of turn B... this turn should be the \\\"next step\\\". Unless each write\u2192activate needs: write (step 1), activate (step 2), THEN next step publish (step 3). This turn's runs were steps 1-3... The last run (after read) is step 4 \u2014 still old!\\n\\nLet me try ONE more run_tests this turn? I already did 3 tool calls... Actually the pattern from the beginning: activation pending \u2192 next turn run works (the testclasses from turn A ran fine in turn B). For MAIN it didn't. The only difference: I wrote main AND activated in the same turn as testclasses? No \u2014 turn A: write testclasses, write main, write llm_http, activate both classes. Turn B: run \u2014 tests new, main old??\\n\\nUnless the MAIN write in turn A silently failed to become part of the activation... The tool said written 11180 chars. read_object NOW (turn C) shows new main. So the write worked. Maybe activation published the testclasses but the main activation op hit an error that wasn't reported? \\\"activated: ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL op_id=... (publish pending)\\\". \\n\\nOR maybe the publish pipeline: after activate, publish happens at the START of the next step; my first run_tests this turn was in the same message block as... no, separate blocks.\\n\\nYou know what \u2014 maybe the issue is that reads and test runs show the last PUBLISHED generation, and publication requires a NEW step after the activation's \\\"pending\\\" state. Timeline steps: [turn B end: activate=pending] [turn C step1: run (still pending \u2192 runs old? but it RAN, didn't error \\\"not published\\\")]. The earlier \\\"ERROR: activation not published yet: finish your turn\\\" happened when I ran twice in one turn. So publish occurs at turn boundary?? Turn C is a new turn \u2014 should be published. But it wasn't!\\n\\nAlternatively \u2014 maybe writes are buffered per-turn and the activate in the SAME turn only activated what was... but testclasses were also written that same turn and DID activate. Both written same turn! testclasses new + main old?? Inconsistent... UNLESS the main include write had a syntax error and activation of main silently kept the old main while activating testclasses? If main had a syntax error, activation would fail entirely...\\n\\nHmm, let me look at my new main code for ABAP syntax issues that open-abap tolerates at write-time but fail at activation/compile: `DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.` inside WHILE \u2014 fine. `lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_i(1).` \u2014 assigning to c from string slice \u2014 fine. Comparisons `lv_ch = `\\\\`` \u2014 comparing c with string \u2014 fine. `IF lv_start + lv_len2 \\u003e lv_len.` fine. `rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_len2).` fine.\\n\\nActually \u2014 WAIT. Maybe the problem: `IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len. RETURN. ENDIF.` \u2014 if delimiter not found, old code returned ''. New: RETURN with rv_ initial '' \u2713.\\n\\nI can't find a syntax error. And read_object succeeded showing full class \u2014 if it were syntactically broken the activator would have complained at activate time (it reported success op_id).\\n\\nNew hypothesis: the test harness ran the OLD generation because \\\"expected_generation\\\":null and generation cccc6ced\u21927a68c5ffe bumps happened. Maybe 7a68c5ffe corresponds to testclasses-only activation (my json_util activate in turn A activated the WHOLE class: both includes). Main should follow.\\n\\nLet me just try re-activating NOW and running next turn. If still old, something deeper. Actually \u2014 better: re-WRITE main (fresh write), then activate, end turn. Maybe the earlier main write got lost/stale in the buffer (e.g., overwritten by a race). A fresh write+activate is the cheapest remedy.\\n\\nAlso consider: could the failure be because write_source was called with include param missing but the tool wrote to testclasses?? \\\"written ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL  (11180 chars)\\\" vs \\\"... testclasses (11095 chars)\\\" \u2014 distinguished correctly. And read shows new main. So write persisted.\\n\\nPlan: rewrite main (same fixed source), activate json_util, finish turn. Next turn: run tests.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007201922201cb42415214065\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_00_json_util DEFINITION PUBLIC FINAL CREATE PUBLIC.\\\\n\\\\n  PUBLIC SECTION.\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS escape\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS codepoint\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS to_int\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS to_hex4\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE i\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS hexval\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS extract_str\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_json     TYPE string\\\\n                iv_name     TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_)  TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS unescape\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_        TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" top-level {...} entries of a JSON array string\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS split_entries\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_arr      TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rt_)  TYPE string_table.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS extract_balanced\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_json     TYPE string\\\\n                iv_key      TYPE string\\\\n                iv_open     TYPE string\\\\n                iv_close    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_)  TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_json_util IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD escape.\\\\n    DATA lv_i TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_cp TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_from TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_len = strlen( iv_ ).\\\\n    WHILE lv_i \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n      lv_ch = iv_+lv_i(1).\\\\n      CASE lv_ch.\\\\n        WHEN `\\\\\\\\`. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\`.\\\\n        WHEN `\\\\\\\"`. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`.\\\\n        WHEN OTHERS.\\\\n          IF lv_ch = |\\\\\\\\n|.\\\\n            rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\n`.\\\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = |\\\\\\\\r|.\\\\n            rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\r`.\\\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = |\\\\\\\\t|.\\\\n            rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\t`.\\\\n          ELSE.\\\\n            \\\\\\\" codepoint from the UTF-8 bytes, read with xstrlen and x(1) offsets: portable to SAP\\\\n            \\\\\\\" (the old strlen/to_upper on an xstring did not compile there) and independent of\\\\n            \\\\\\\" cl_abap_conv_out_ce=\\u003euccpi, which is wrong in open-abap-core (high byte * 255)\\\\n            \\\\\\\" a character outside the BMP (emoji) is two UTF-16 units: alone, a unit fails to convert\\\\n            \\\\\\\" on SAP (CX_SY_CONVERSION_CODEPAGE) and becomes U+FFFD in OSG; take the pair together\\\\n            lv_cp = codepoint( lv_ch ).\\\\n            IF lv_cp = 65533 AND lv_i + 1 \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n              lv_from = lv_i.\\\\n              lv_cp = codepoint( substring( val = iv_ off = lv_from len = 2 ) ).\\\\n              IF lv_cp \\u003e= 65536.\\\\n                lv_cp = lv_cp - 65536.\\\\n                rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\u` \\u0026\\u0026 to_hex4( 55296 + lv_cp DIV 1024 ) \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\u` \\u0026\\u0026 to_hex4( 56320 + lv_cp MOD 1024 ).\\\\n                lv_i = lv_i + 2.\\\\n                CONTINUE.\\\\n              ENDIF.\\\\n              lv_cp = 65533.\\\\n            ENDIF.\\\\n            IF lv_cp \\u003e= 32 AND lv_cp \\u003c 128.\\\\n              rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 lv_ch.\\\\n            ELSE.\\\\n              rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\u` \\u0026\\u0026 to_hex4( lv_cp ).\\\\n            ENDIF.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n      ENDCASE.\\\\n      lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\\\n    ENDWHILE.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD codepoint.\\\\n    DATA lv_x TYPE xstring.\\\\n    DATA lv_b TYPE x LENGTH 1.\\\\n    DATA lv_b0 TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_b1 TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_b2 TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_b3 TYPE i.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" a lone UTF-16 surrogate does not convert on SAP; caught here because the method declares\\\\n    \\\\\\\" no RAISING (outside it the exception would arrive as CX_SY_NO_HANDLER)\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        lv_x = cl_abap_conv_codepage=\\u003ecreate_out( )-\\u003econvert( iv_ ).\\\\n      CATCH cx_root.\\\\n        rv_ = 65533.\\\\n        RETURN.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n    lv_b = lv_x+0(1).\\\\n    lv_b0 = lv_b.\\\\n    CASE xstrlen( lv_x ).\\\\n      WHEN 1.\\\\n        rv_ = lv_b0.\\\\n      WHEN 2.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+1(1).\\\\n        lv_b1 = lv_b.\\\\n        rv_ = ( lv_b0 - 192 ) * 64 + ( lv_b1 - 128 ).\\\\n      WHEN 3.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+1(1).\\\\n        lv_b1 = lv_b.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+2(1).\\\\n        lv_b2 = lv_b.\\\\n        rv_ = ( lv_b0 - 224 ) * 4096 + ( lv_b1 - 128 ) * 64 + ( lv_b2 - 128 ).\\\\n      WHEN 4.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+1(1).\\\\n        lv_b1 = lv_b.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+2(1).\\\\n        lv_b2 = lv_b.\\\\n        lv_b = lv_x+3(1).\\\\n        lv_b3 = lv_b.\\\\n        rv_ = ( lv_b0 - 240 ) * 262144 + ( lv_b1 - 128 ) * 4096 + ( lv_b2 - 128 ) * 64 + ( lv_b3 - 128 ).\\\\n      WHEN OTHERS.\\\\n        rv_ = 65533.\\\\n    ENDCASE.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_int.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" hex pair -\\u003e int\\\\n    rv_ = hexval( substring( val = iv_ off = 0 len = 1 ) ) * 16\\\\n          + hexval( substring( val = iv_ off = 1 len = 1 ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD to_hex4.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" 4-digit uppercase hex (was decimal: 1046 -\\u003e '1046' instead of '0416')\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_hex TYPE string VALUE `0123456789ABCDEF`.\\\\n    DATA lv_n TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_d TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_n = iv_.\\\\n    DO 4 TIMES.\\\\n      lv_d = lv_n MOD 16.\\\\n      rv_ = substring( val = c_hex off = lv_d len = 1 ) \\u0026\\u0026 rv_.\\\\n      lv_n = lv_n DIV 16.\\\\n    ENDDO.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD hexval.\\\\n    CASE to_upper( substring( val = iv_ off = 0 len = 1 ) ).\\\\n      WHEN '0'. rv_ = 0. WHEN '1'. rv_ = 1. WHEN '2'. rv_ = 2. WHEN '3'. rv_ = 3.\\\\n      WHEN '4'. rv_ = 4. WHEN '5'. rv_ = 5. WHEN '6'. rv_ = 6. WHEN '7'. rv_ = 7.\\\\n      WHEN '8'. rv_ = 8. WHEN '9'. rv_ = 9. WHEN 'A'. rv_ = 10. WHEN 'B'. rv_ = 11.\\\\n      WHEN 'C'. rv_ = 12. WHEN 'D'. rv_ = 13. WHEN 'E'. rv_ = 14. WHEN 'F'. rv_ = 15.\\\\n    ENDCASE.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD extract_str.\\\\n    DATA(lv_re) = '\\\\\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 iv_name \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"((?:[^\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\]|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.)*)\\\\\\\"'.\\\\n    FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF PCRE lv_re IN iv_json SUBMATCHES rv_.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD unescape.\\\\n    DATA lv_i TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_j TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_len = strlen( iv_ ).\\\\n    WHILE lv_i \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n      IF iv_+lv_i(1) = `\\\\\\\\` AND lv_i + 1 \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n        lv_j = lv_i + 1.\\\\n        CASE iv_+lv_j(1).\\\\n          WHEN `n`. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n|.\\\\n          WHEN `r`. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\r|.\\\\n          WHEN `t`. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\t|.\\\\n          WHEN `u`.\\\\n            \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\uXXXX -\\u003e character (was: only 5 ASCII codepoints, Cyrillic stayed escaped)\\\\n            DATA lv_hex TYPE string.\\\\n            DATA lv_char TYPE string.\\\\n            IF lv_j + 4 \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n              lv_hex = iv_+lv_j(5).\\\\n              lv_hex = lv_hex+1(4).\\\\n              TRY.\\\\n                  lv_char = cl_abap_conv_in_ce=\\u003euccp( to_upper( lv_hex ) ).\\\\n                  rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 lv_char.\\\\n                CATCH cx_root.\\\\n                  rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\u` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_hex.\\\\n              ENDTRY.\\\\n              lv_i = lv_i + 4.\\\\n            ENDIF.\\\\n          WHEN OTHERS. rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 iv_+lv_j(1).\\\\n        ENDCASE.\\\\n        lv_i = lv_i + 2.\\\\n      ELSE.\\\\n        rv_ = rv_ \\u0026\\u0026 iv_+lv_i(1).\\\\n        lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n    ENDWHILE.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_entries.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" top-level {...} entries of a JSON array string; defensive: every access is clamped.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" String-aware: a quote opens/closes a JSON string only when the backslash run\\\\n    \\\\\\\" before it is even (odd = escaped \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"); braces inside a string value are data,\\\\n    \\\\\\\" not structure. A single '{' or '}' in a tool-call argument used to keep the\\\\n    \\\\\\\" depth counter open, so the first entry swallowed the rest of the array and\\\\n    \\\\\\\" every following tool call was lost (found by SPLIT_BRACE_IN_STRING).\\\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_len = strlen( iv_arr ).\\\\n    DATA lv_i TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_run TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_in TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\\\n    DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_start TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_n TYPE i.\\\\n    WHILE lv_i \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n      DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\\\n      lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_i(1).\\\\n      IF lv_ch = `\\\\\\\\`.\\\\n        lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\\\n        lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\\\n        CONTINUE.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      IF lv_ch = '\\\\\\\"'.\\\\n        IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\\\n          IF lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_false.\\\\n          ELSE.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n      ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false.\\\\n        IF lv_ch = '{'.\\\\n          IF lv_depth = 0.\\\\n            lv_start = lv_i.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = '}'.\\\\n          IF lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\\\n            lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\\\n            IF lv_depth = 0.\\\\n              lv_n = lv_i - lv_start + 1.\\\\n              IF lv_start + lv_n \\u003e lv_len.\\\\n                lv_n = lv_len - lv_start.\\\\n              ENDIF.\\\\n              IF lv_n \\u003e 0.\\\\n                APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_n) TO rt_.\\\\n              ENDIF.\\\\n            ENDIF.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      lv_run = 0.\\\\n      lv_i = lv_i + 1.\\\\n    ENDWHILE.\\\\n    IF lv_depth \\u003e 0 AND lv_start \\u003c lv_len AND lv_start \\u003c= lv_i.\\\\n      \\\\\\\" unclosed trailing object: clamp to the end, as before\\\\n      lv_n = lv_len - lv_start.\\\\n      APPEND iv_arr+lv_start(lv_n) TO rt_.\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD extract_balanced.\\\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA(lv_pat) = '\\\\\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 iv_key \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\\\\\"'.\\\\n    FIND lv_pat IN iv_json MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\\\n    DATA lv_rest TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_rest = iv_json+lv_off.\\\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_len = strlen( lv_rest ).\\\\n    \\\\\\\" 1) find the opening delimiter outside JSON strings (a delimiter inside a\\\\n    \\\\\\\"    string value is data, not structure)\\\\n    DATA lv_start TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_run TYPE i VALUE 0.\\\\n    DATA lv_in TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\\\n    WHILE lv_start \\u003c lv_len.\\\\n      DATA lv_ch TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\\\n      lv_ch = lv_rest+lv_start(1).\\\\n      IF lv_ch = `\\\\\\\\`.\\\\n        lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\\\n        lv_start = lv_start + 1.\\\\n        CONTINUE.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      IF lv_ch = '\\\\\\\"'.\\\\n        IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\\\n          IF lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_false.\\\\n          ELSE.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n      ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false AND lv_ch = iv_open.\\\\n        lv_run = 0.\\\\n        EXIT.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      lv_run = 0.\\\\n      lv_start = lv_start + 1.\\\\n    ENDWHILE.\\\\n    IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len. RETURN. ENDIF.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" 2) balanced scan; a quote toggles string state only after an even backslash\\\\n    \\\\\\\"    run (odd = escaped \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), braces/brackets inside strings do not count.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"    Blind counting broke on arguments like lv_open = '{'. (unclosed depth,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"    value ran past the object into the next JSON members)\\\\n    DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 1.\\\\n    DATA lv_pos TYPE i.\\\\n    lv_pos = lv_start. \\\\\\\" VALUE takes only a constant on SAP (OSG accepted a variable)\\\\n    WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\\\n      lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\\\n      DATA lv_c TYPE c LENGTH 1.\\\\n      lv_c = lv_rest+lv_pos(1).\\\\n      IF lv_c = `\\\\\\\\`.\\\\n        lv_run = lv_run + 1.\\\\n        CONTINUE.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      IF lv_c = '\\\\\\\"'.\\\\n        IF lv_run MOD 2 = 0.\\\\n          IF lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_false.\\\\n          ELSE.\\\\n            lv_in = abap_true.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n      ELSEIF lv_in = abap_false.\\\\n        IF lv_c = iv_open.\\\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\\\n        ELSEIF lv_c = iv_close.\\\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n      ENDIF.\\\\n      lv_run = 0.\\\\n    ENDWHILE.\\\\n    DATA(lv_len2) = lv_pos - lv_start + 1.\\\\n    IF lv_start + lv_len2 \\u003e lv_len.\\\\n      lv_len2 = lv_len - lv_start.\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n    IF lv_len2 \\u003e 0.\\\\n      rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_len2).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227999981402062031\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227999981402062031\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":38476,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":33600},\"output_tokens\":7739,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":4329},\"total_tokens\":46215}}
