{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791375817,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072021378a5c7c1858884171\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The same generation_id \\\"7a68c5ffe680388b\\\" keeps appearing \u2014 the test run is hitting the same cached/previous generation. The activation said \\\"publish pending \u2014 new code live in next step\\\", but multiple subsequent turns still run the old generation. Something is stuck: the run_tests output always shows \\\"expected_generation\\\": null and generation_id 7a68c5ff... even after multiple activations (op_id 49dbe00d...).\\n\\nHmm \u2014 maybe the publish requires the turn to END after activation, which I did (I ended the turn with a summary). Then next turn run_tests should use the new code. But the generation_id hasn't changed since the run in the turn where I read the object. Wait \u2014 let me check history: the red run showing 36 methods had generation 9f337c1e (first), then cccc6ce